    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for LawDog hinges on exploiting the soft matchup against Gusto, with **Geraldo Perdomo** (69.91) and **Luis Arraez** (67.31) serving as our primary engines. **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits from a massive 19% boost due to the favorable SP skill matchup, providing a high-floor opportunity to accumulate counting stats from the #2 spot. Similarly, **Luis Arraez** earns his top-tier status by pairing his elite contact profile with a generous SP matchup; combined with **Jung Hoo Lee** (63.73) and **Matt Chapman** (61.19), we are heavily invested in the Gusto fade. **Tyler Freeman** is our surprise value play today (63.09), as a 14% park factor boost mitigates a neutral platoon outlook, making him an essential start despite the moderate SP_xERA.\n\nThe decision to bench **Jeremiah Jackson** (39.89) was the most difficult call on the docket, as he missed our 40-point efficiency floor by a mere fraction of a point. His prospects were stifled by a brutal matchup against Sheehan and a suboptimal #9 spot in the batting order, which collectively dragged his projections below the threshold required to displace our current starters. We continue to monitor the status of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who remains sidelined on the IL, while **Lawrence Butler** and **Yainer Diaz** were excluded today due to assumed rest cycles. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the risks inherent in today's matchups. **Bryson Stott** (42.65) is a high-risk play today, hampered by an elite opposing catcher's pop time and a defensive hold strategy that significantly suppresses SB opportunities, forcing him into a pure counting-stat role. Furthermore, both **Gavin Sheets** (46.12) and **Taylor Ward** (43.98) are running close to our bench floor; they face tough assignments against Eovaldi and Sheehan respectively. If the wind shifts or late lineup changes further compress their outlooks, we will prioritize defensive substitutions to protect our daily game caps.",
